WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.760
What's up guys my name is Colin McNeil, for theScore esports.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.000
Last week ex-Halo player and current Fortnite streamer Ninja made mainstream

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.080
headlines when he queued with Drake, Travis Scott and Juju Smith-Schuster, breaking a

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.440
lot of Twitch records in the process.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:22.340
Now I know, you and I could probably not care less about the latest celebrity gossip.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.540
But you gotta admit, when someone who's mainstream famous, or just famous in a

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.360
community that isn't gaming, streams. It's kinda hype.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:36.440
With that in mind we thought this would be the
perfect opportunity to bring you The Top 10 Celebrities

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.360
who have streamed on Twitch.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.120
Well guys, we decided to start our list off
on a high note for this one, with the D-O-Double

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:54.260
G himself Snoop Dogg streaming battle royale title SOS in January of 2018.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:01:07.060
(Stream)

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:13.680
Now let me blunt here, it appears that Snoop Dogg wasn't actually playing the game so much as he was

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.560
watching, reacting and controlling the mic.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.140
We just hope that doesn't cause his future streaming career to go up in smoke.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:38.140
(Stream)

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:44.580
Next up on our list, Felicia Day is widely known as one of the queens of the nerds.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.180
She’s most famous for her role as the producer of The Guild, a series that is based off of

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.659
her life as a gamer.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:55.869
Felicia was also a member of the cast of Buffy: The Vampire Slayer and Supernatural among

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:56.660
others.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.800
In recent years Felicia has built her stream on Twitch playing a variety of games

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.280
(Stream)

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.400
Including: Rise of the Tomb Raider and Dragon Age: Inquisition.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:19.400
(Stream)

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.860
Number eight on our list might be the only member of this Top 10 that’s actually competed at

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.040
an esports event.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:32.000
Hayward has always been an advocate for esports
and even competed in the IGN Pro League during

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.800
the NBA lockout in 2011.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.340
Alright Gordon let's get you into shape! Now what league are you in?

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.580
The NBA!

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.160
I meant in StarCraft II

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:42.940
Oh, Gold.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:47.000
When he hits the the rift, Hayward can be found in the top lane playing champions like

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.660
Tryndamere and outplaying his lane opponents like we see here:

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:59.980
(Stream)

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:05.440
R&amp;B and hip-hop performer T-Pain was one of the first celebrities to make their mark on

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.840
Overwatch after the game came out.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:13.060
The “Buy you a Drank” singer’s on-stream
antics are just as hilarious as you’d expect.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:19.920
(Stream)

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:25.400
He can be found playing a variety of heros,
from Junkrat to Lucio to Hanzo.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.940
(Stream)

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.840
Famous DJ, producer and musician Deadmau5, comes in at number six and he's likely the celebrity who’s taken

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.980
the biggest dive into Twitch.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.160
Deadmau5 streams almost everyday with a lot of it lately being PUBG.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:50.240
(Stream)

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.960
He’s also found a unique way to combine
his career with his Twitch personality

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.460
by streaming himself working on and creating music.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:04.480
Of all of the members on this list Deadmau5 is definitely the one most entrenched in Twitch

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:05.800
and streaming culture.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:20.160
(Stream)

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.960
Coming in at number five

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:27.740
Quinton “Rampage” Jackson is a former
UFC Light Heavyweight champion and has recently

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.160
been streaming PlayerUnknown’s Battlegrounds.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:35.900
(Stream)

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.720
Jackson has even been known to get some winner winner chicken dinners, proving that he can

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.660
go on a rampage in and out of the ring.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:53.180
(Stream)

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:58.340
Lupe Fiasco is the second hip-hop star to
touch down on our list.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:03.240
The “Superstar” rapper has been a huge
supporter of the Fighting Game Community for

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.540
years now and is more than just a Street Fighter fan, he’s a player.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:14.380
(Stream)

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.440
He even allowed Capcom to use a song from his newest album for Colleen’s announcement

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:20.260
trailer.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:23.200
(Trailer)

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:28.280
His biggest gaming moment was certainly his showmatch against Daigo at the Street Fighter V

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.740
release party.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:35.500
(Stream)

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.560
Taking the third spot on this list is

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:43.560
Rick Fox, a true OG of the celebrity dive
into esports and an ex NBA player

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.580
with the Boston Celtics and Los Angeles Lakers.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.400
He’s really done it all in esports from
streaming

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:59.040
(Stream)

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.620
to becoming part-owner of Echo Fox.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:07.000
Rick Fox is known for that winning smile and has really entrenched himself in the scene over

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.880
the last few years.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:13.160
Back in February, Fox streamed
for the first time with his son Kyle.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:17.980
(Stream)

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.620
Taking the coveted number two spot on this list

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:26.580
Mia Khalfia has quickly become one of the
most notable online personalities out there.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.680
The former adult actress turned Washington
sports personality and COMPLEX talk show host

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:35.440
has recently started doing IRL streams.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:38.700
(Stream)

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.660
She’s streamed herself doing everything from cooking to

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:44.280
hanging out on the couch playing NBA 2K.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:48.380
(Stream)

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.960
Well I bet you didn’t see this one coming.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:56.820
Our number one is last week’s record-setting
stream featuring Ninja, and rappers Drake,

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:01.820
Travis Scott and Pittsburgh Steelers wide
receiver JuJu Smith-Schuster.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:07.740
After initially stumbling to get their comms going the stream quickly smashed Twitch viewership

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:15.700
records and got as high as 630,000 concurrent,
smashing Dr. DisRespects previous record of

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.960
388,000.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:26.380
(Stream)

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:30.000
In what was arguably one of the most iconic moments

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:36.370
in Twitch’s history, the 6 god blessed viewers
all over the world with some memorable stream

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:37.340
highlights.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:45.340
(Stream)

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:50.200
I’d like to dub this particular stream “Views
from Titled Towers”

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:57.380
(Stream)

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.860
Well guys that’s our list. But if your favourite celebrity stream did not make our Top 10

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:05.400
Just flame us in the comments or something okay?

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:10.080
Thanks for watching. If you want more great content just like this, be sure to hit the subscribe button.

